Package: viridisSYR
Type: Package
Title: Syracuse-Anchored Variant of the Viridis 'Plasma' Colour Scale
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Nina R.", "Benway", , "53921196+nrgslp@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A continuous colour scale in the viridis family that starts at
    Syracuse University navy (#000E54), passes through the viridis 'plasma'
    purple, then through Syracuse University orange (#F76700), and ends at the
    viridis 'plasma' yellow. The scale is codified as a fixed 1001-colour map,
    so the Syracuse colours can be retrieved directly from it. Includes
    'ggplot2' scales, functions that return the colours (and the data values)
    at the key points, and tools to evaluate the scale with the criteria used
    to design 'viridis' (perceptual uniformity and lightness order in
    CAM02-UCS, grayscale and colour-vision-deficiency behaviour) and to
    compare it with 'plasma'. Not affiliated with or endorsed by Syracuse
    University; the two Syracuse hex codes are used as published brand colours.
